'''Onji Shrine''' (恩智神社) is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|ja|神社|12=draft}} located in {{ill|Onji Nakamachi, Yao, Osaka|ja|恩智中町|12=draft}}, {{ill|Yao, Osaka|ja|八尾市|12=draft}}, {{ill|Osaka Prefecture|ja|大阪府|12=draft}}. It is an ancient shrine recorded as a {{ill|Shikinai-sha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|12=draft}} ({{ill|Myōjin Taisha|ja|名神大社|fr|Myōjin Taisha|zh|名神大社|12=draft}}) and is traditionally considered the Ninomiya or second Ranked shrine of {{ill|Kawachi Province|ja|河内国|12=draft}}. Under the {{ill|Modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines|ja|近代社格制度|1=Modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines|12=draft}}, it was classified as a {{ill|Prefectural shrine|ja|府社|12=draft}}. The shrine’s [[Shinshi|messengers]] are said to be rabbits and dragons.

== Gallery ==
<gallery>
File:Onji-jinja,_kofun.jpg|link=File:Onji-jinja,_kofun.jpg|Main hall (left) and the ancient tomb behind it (right back)
File:Onji-shrine02.JPG|link=File:Onji-shrine02.JPG|Akaido (Seimei Water)<br /><br />{{Small|This well is associated with the monk Kūkai and is said to predict the weather by becoming cloudy before rain.}}
File:Onji-jinja,_entrance.jpg|link=File:Onji-jinja,_entrance.jpg|Shrine entrance
File:Onji-jinja,_torii.jpg|link=File:Onji-jinja,_torii.jpg|Torii gate
File:Yao_City_Onji_Nakacho_3-chome_excavation,_Decorated_Bronze_Bell_(J-9212).JPG|Decorated bronze bell excavated from Onji Nakacho 3-chome, Yao City<br /><br />{{Small|Displayed at the Tokyo National Museum.}}
</gallery>

